---
// A third ordinary page, and it exists to make one rule visible: a page is
// live only when BOTH halves are there — this file, and a published row
// carrying the same slug. Creating the row in the dashboard alone gives a
// page that answers 404, which is exactly what happened while writing this.
//
// Its row must exist in the dashboard with the slug `contact`, and be
// published — otherwise this route answers 404, deliberately.
export const prerender = false

import { loadPage } from "../lib/loadPage"
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro"
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro"
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro"
import "../styles/global.css"

const { page } = await loadPage(Astro, "a-propos")
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="fr">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <PageHead page={page} />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-white text-ink antialiased">
    <SiteHeader />
    {page === null ? (
      <main class="mx-auto flex min-h-svh max-w-2xl flex-col items-center justify-center gap-3 px-6 text-center">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">404</h1>
        <p class="text-ink-mid">Cette page n'existe pas.</p>
      </main>
    ) : (
      <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">{page.title}</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-ink-mid">
          Troisième page d’exemple. Elle existe parce que ce fichier existe — créer sa ligne dans l’administration ne suffit pas. Le titre ci-dessus, les champs
          SEO et GEO, et la publication de cette page se règlent dans
          l'administration ; tout le reste s'écrit ici, en code.
        </p>
      </main>
    )}
    <SiteFooter />
  </body>
</html>
